# FreeBSD ports files of lang/php82 that are NOT applied, with the reason.
# Format: "<port file>: <reason>"; listed in the branch README and in the release notes.
# Documentation only: editing this file does not rebuild the branch.
patch-configure.ac: three hunks are the ports build layout, which makes php_config.h include ext/php_config.h that only the port's Makefile creates (a hand build fails without it), drops the configure pthreads check and sets the ports' PEAR include_path, and two do not matter here: the nanosleep hunk (libc before librt) would only drop a NEEDED librt.so.1 (librt is part of the base system), and php-src has no include/ for the header hunk to leave out. The port has no ifunc hunk (lang/php83 has one: compat-freebsd-ifunc.patch of 8.3), so configure skips the ifunc and target checks on FreeBSD, as in the official package
patch-ext_hash_xxhash_xxhash.h: PowerPC VSX (AltiVec) and s390x only; no effect on amd64
patch-ext_mysqli_mysqli__api.c: ports split packaging of ext/mysqli (built alone with phpize, where the ext/mysqlnd headers are missing); not needed when building from the full source tree
patch-ext_mysqli_mysqli__nonapi.c: ports split packaging of ext/mysqli (built alone with phpize, where the ext/mysqlnd headers are missing); not needed when building from the full source tree
patch-ext_mysqli_mysqli__prop.c: ports split packaging of ext/mysqli (built alone with phpize, where the ext/mysqlnd headers are missing); not needed when building from the full source tree
patch-ext_pcre_pcre2lib_sljit_sljitConfigInternal.h: PowerPC 32-bit only; no effect on amd64
php_fpm.in: the rc.d script of the port, not a source patch; your own rc.d scripts stay in use
